# Stage4 BASE package list — Orange Pi 5 / Orange Pi 5 Plus (Rockchip RK3588/
# RK3588S, arm64) LIGHT desktop. One atom per line; lines starting with # are
# ignored.
#
# This is the BASE (always-installed) set: kernel sources, U-Boot tooling, the
# mesh/provisioning dependencies, and a hardened base system. The lean DESKTOP
# stack is a SEPARATE list (packages-desktop.list) appended by the builder
# unconditionally (this platform has ONE role — no headless/none toggle the way
# Frite has --desktop none; see the builder header).
#
# NOTE on the RK3588 boot chain (EXPERIMENTAL — see specs-orangepi5/README.md):
#   * Boots via mainline U-Boot (orangepi-5-rk3588s_defconfig / orangepi-5-plus-
#     rk3588_defconfig) needing a Rockchip DDR-init blob (TPL/SPL) and a TF-A
#     BL31 blob from rkbin (mainline TF-A does not yet support RK3588) — see the
#     builder's header comment for the full chain. U-Boot's distro-boot then
#     scans the first partition for /extlinux/extlinux.conf, same mechanism as
#     Frite. There is NO raspberrypi-firmware blob and NO config.txt.
#   * The board-specific DTB ships from the KERNEL build (gentoo-sources /
#     mainline), NOT from a vendor firmware package — see the builder's
#     "DTB" section. The U-Boot binary itself is vendored/fetched by the
#     builder (needs the proprietary rkbin DDR/BL31 blobs to be flashable).

# ── Kernel sources (mainline; RK3588/RK3588S device trees are upstream) ────
# The rk3588s-orangepi-5 / rk3588-orangepi-5-plus DTS entries are mainline as of
# recent kernel releases (this fragment's HDMI/VOP2 note in
# hardened-desktop.config flags 6.13+ as the practical floor for working HDMI
# output — VERIFY the actual gentoo-sources version pulled at build time).
sys-kernel/gentoo-sources
sys-kernel/linux-firmware

# ── Bootloader tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# u-boot-tools provides mkimage (FIT/extlinux) used to assemble the boot blob;
# the actual U-Boot binary for the board is built/fetched by the builder (see
# --uboot-url; needs Rockchip's rkbin DDR-init + TF-A BL31 blobs to be
# flashable — mainline U-Boot alone is not, mirroring Frite's Amlogic FIP/BL31
# situation).
dev-embedded/u-boot-tools

# ── Board hardware / storage ──────────────────────────────────────
sys-block/parted
sys-apps/usbutils
sys-apps/i2c-tools
sys-apps/util-linux
sys-fs/e2fsprogs
sys-fs/dosfstools
sys-apps/pciutils

# ── Networking ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
net-misc/networkmanager
net-misc/openssh
net-firewall/iptables
net-misc/socat
# Egress VPN (split-tunnel, fail-closed) — wg-quick (WireGuard, first-class) +
# openvpn (fallback) for the node-level hugmesh-egress-vpn OpenRC service
# (DEFAULT-OFF; same plumbing as every other client image).
net-vpn/wireguard-tools
net-vpn/openvpn
# WiFi supplicant is present so the M.2/onboard AP6275P radio CAN work once a
# working brcmfmac path exists, but WiFi is OFF BY DEFAULT (hardened posture;
# mainline WiFi support on this exact module is ROUGH as of the research behind
# this platform — see specs-orangepi5/README.md). Ethernet + the tailnet are
# the primary, reliable path.
net-wireless/wpa_supplicant

# ── System ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
app-admin/sudo
sys-process/cronie
sys-apps/haveged
app-editors/nano
app-misc/screen
app-misc/jq

# ── Hardened / security (SELinux LSM) ──────────────────────────────
# Same posture as the cluster images: SELinux is the LSM. The policy packages'
# pkg_postinst runs the TARGET `semodule`, which can't execute under an aarch64
# cross-emerge — so the base policy is LOADED AT FIRST BOOT (native) by
# keys-provision (shared engine). See docs/SECURITY.md.
sec-policy/selinux-base
sec-policy/selinux-base-policy
sys-apps/policycoreutils
sys-apps/semodule-utils
sys-apps/checkpolicy
sys-libs/libselinux
sys-libs/libseccomp
sys-process/audit

# NOTE: sys-fs/cryptsetup is NOT listed here — it is appended by the builder
# ONLY when --encrypt-root is set (mirrors specs-frite/portage/packages.list's
# equivalent comment); install-orangepi5.sh is what actually runs
# luksFormat/open/close on the target hardware at install time.

# ── KEYS USB provisioning + attached storage ──────────────────────
# Same first-boot provisioning engine as every other client image: jq parses the
# manifests, dosfstools/util-linux handle the FAT32 KEYS partition + blkid.
net-fs/nfs-utils
net-fs/cifs-utils

# NOTE: headscale + tailscale are NOT emerged here. They are installed as
# upstream static arm64 binaries by build-orangepi5-stage4.sh (the "mesh"
# phase), identical to the Frite/RPi5 images. See --skip-mesh / --skip-tailscale.
